## Important Concepts to Understand

You do not need to become a full-time DevOps engineer to deploy Python applications.

You should understand:

    Linux
    Bash
    SSH
    Processes
    Environment variables
    Docker
    Docker Compose
    Nginx
    Gunicorn
    CI/CD
    GitHub Actions
    DNS
    HTTPS
    Production databases
    Logging
    Monitoring
    Basic cloud infrastructure

You should be able to look at:

    User
      ↓
    DNS
      ↓
    Server
      ↓
    Nginx
      ↓
    Gunicorn
      ↓
    Python
      ↓
    Database

and understand what each component is doing.

---

## Final Goal

You should be able to take:

    Python application
          ↓
    Git repository
          ↓
    Cloud/server
          ↓
    Production configuration
          ↓
    Domain
          ↓
    HTTPS
          ↓
    Public website/API

and understand the entire journey.

The key idea is:

    Development:
        "It works on my computer."

    Deployment:
        "It works on a server."

    Production:
        "It works reliably, securely and
         can be monitored and maintained."

You do not need to memorise every Linux command or AWS service.

The important skill is understanding how the pieces fit together and being able to deploy, troubleshoot and maintain a real Python application.